      "text": "I fixed the code in `src/` to match SPEC.md, and the 5 public tests still pass. I did not add tests for the new behaviour, so the fixes below are untested.\n\n- **Receiving** (`inventory.ts`): receiving into an existing lot id now adds to its quantity instead of replacing it.\n- **Availability** (`inventory.ts`): expired lots no longer count towards a sku's available stock.\n- **Lot order** (`inventory.ts`): lots with the same expiry are now used in ascending id order. It was descending.\n- **Reserving** (`orders.ts`):\n  - Repeated skus in an order's lines are now summed before reserving.\n  - A failed order now releases everything it had reserved. Before, it released only part of it.\n- **Backorder retries** (`backorder.ts`): cancelled orders are dropped from the queue and never reserved again.\n- **Shipping** (`warehouse.ts`): the limit is now the units still reserved for that sku. It was the original line quantity, so repeated shipping could exceed what was reserved.\n- **Cancelling** (`warehouse.ts`): it now releases only the units still reserved. Before, it also released units that had already shipped.\n- **Returns** (`warehouse.ts`): units go back to the lot only if it can still be used that day, meaning its expiry is on or after the day. The old check was off by one day.",
